Definitions .-(1) In these regulations, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)
"Act" means the Insurance Act, 1938 (
4 of 1938
);
(b)
"approved Institution" means an Institution engaged in education and/or training particularly in the area of insurance
sales, service and marketing, approved by the Authority;
(c)
"Authority" means the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority established under the provisions of section 3 of
the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority Act, 1999 (
41 of 1999
);
(d)
"certification" means the process by which a specified person of the corporate agent, who has successfully undergone
practical training and passed the required examination, is issued a certificate entitling him to solicit and procure
insurance business on behalf of the corporate agent;
(e)
"composite corporate agent" means a corporate agent who holds a license to act as an insurance agent for a life insurer
and a general insurer;
(f)
"corporate agent" means any person specified in clause (k) and licensed to act as such;

(b)
disclose his license/certificate to the prospect on demand;
(c)
disseminate the requisite information in respect of insurance products offered for sale by his insurer and take into
